Changes in version 2.1.81
SQLite revival (2026-10, branch sqlite-revival):
 - saveOmicsViewerDb now persists the app-ready view: wide GS|* gene-set
   columns are moved into the GS table at save (tallGS), so database
   datasets carry working gene sets (ORA/fGSEA/GSList tabs were dead on
   this path) and the feature table is no longer polluted with hundreds
   of membership columns
 - metadata attributes round trip through the new attrs table:
   user-defined quickViews, volcanoCategories, cormat, S6.6_drc,
   precomputed expression dendrograms (rowDendrogram/colDendrogram);
   object-level attributes are served through the getAx seam at both
   attr() call sites (cormat in L0, S6.6_drc in the result space)
 - type fidelity: factor levels, logicals and Dates are rebuilt from
   recorded column-type metadata; NaN normalizes to NA at save (SQLite
   cannot represent NaN); getExprs no longer routes doubles through a
   character matrix
 - connection hygiene: readESVObj opens validated READ-ONLY connections
   (missing files are not silently created, non-database files are
   rejected with a clear error) and the app closes dataset connections
   on dataset switch and session end
 - legacy (pre-2.1.81) databases are recovered on read: wide GS|*
   columns are converted back into the gene-set annotation; a meta
   table marks the schema version
 - save atomicity: all writes run in one transaction; guards reject a
   real 'rowname' column, duplicated column names and unsupported
   column classes before the file is touched; a stale exprsimpute
   table no longer survives a re-save without imputed values
 - tallGS preserves ALL fData attributes (volcanoCategories etc. were
   dropped together with the wide gene-set columns on the .RDS path)
 - docs: ?saveOmicsViewerDb documents the schema; ?prepOmicsViewer
   SQLite caveats lifted

Changes in version 2.1.80
UI-mimic hardening program (F1-F8, 2026-10, branch llm-ui-hardening):
 - F1: set_scatter_view isolate fix - semantic scatter writes work on
   fresh sessions (was dead 3/3 with a misleading rejection)
 - F2/WP-4+5: stub-drop root cause found (client-side discard during
   an active stream; the abort-settle amplifier) with permanent
   transport flight recorders (chat_submit_seen, janitor_run),
   stuck-stream detection and loud notifications - silent message
   loss is now visible and diagnosed
 - F8/WP-6: composer delivery watchdog - undelivered submissions
   become visible after 10 s with a server-owned Retry that re-drives
   the submission through shinychat's own update_user_input
 - F3/WP-1: search_annotations with an empty query returns a bounded
   annotation category catalog (~3.5 KB for demo.RDS) - column
   enumeration went from 5-8 blind synonym calls to 1-2
 - F5/WP-2 (+amendments): find_controls empty query returns the
   per-tab capability digest; fuzzy hits rank by matched-word count;
   byte-shaped payloads never trip the codec truncation marker
 - F6/WP-3: figure filter errors list the figure's available columns
   and featureId/sampleId resolve to the reserved id columns
 - F4/WP-7: new panel_results state section - the head of the ORA/
   fGSEA result tables (key columns, rounded, ~3 KB) is readable by
   the assistant after a run; uncomputed panels return explicit
   not_run notes; result tables never leak into snapshots
 - F7/WP-8: progress line under the composer (submission / model
   responding / step N: tool, per-turn counter) + soft [PACE] tool-
   call guidance in the system prompt
 - WP-9: full guard board green (Tier A 120/120, new
   test_agentPanelResults 26, sweep gate PASS 344 after the gene-
   picker vocabulary repair of a pre-existing e8554e7 regression)

Changes in version 2.1.79
widget-sweep remediation program (WP-0..WP-G2, 2026-10):
 - WP-0: the exhaustive 337-case agent widget sweep doubled as the
   one-command regression gate (NOT_CRAN=true
   tests/e2e_agent/widget_sweep/run_regression.sh; surgical baseline
   refresh workflow)
 - WP-A: choices providers that declare a provider but return empty
   now reject with a self-describing reason instead of accepting
   anything; dynamic-heatmap choices are activation-independent
   (dataset-backed choice sources, selection-preserving choice
   re-pushes)
 - WP-B/WP-B2: the F4 "table columns anomaly" and the F6 expr-heatmap
   congestion were disproven as harness measurement artifacts - no
   product change; the harness read-back bug was fixed
 - WP-C: action tier - widget_action()/store_register_action()/
   store_action_run(), 10 module buttons operable through the new
   run_control tool (snapshot lifecycle and dataset switching
   PERMANENTLY excluded; destructive actions never agent-runnable)
 - WP-D: the four attr4 searchon gene-highlight pickers are store
   bindings (attr4.search_value; joint cascade+values patches valid
   through the effective view)
 - WP-E: F5 dead-end chains - precondition notes on conditional
   bindings; survival-censor R-M7 push ordering fixed (a push landing
   before the view renders is no longer dropped); stringdb/batch/
   censor chains probe-verified end to end
 - WP-F: categorical-axis freeze remediation CANCELLED by decision -
   the 2702-category freeze is accepted as-is
 - WP-G1: every capability record carries tab/effect (+group on
   cascades); 17 panel records from the sr-only prose; find_controls
   gains a bounded fuzzy fallback
 - WP-G2: snapshot-lifecycle + dataset-selector sweep cases carry the
   explicit excluded-by-policy status; downloads/export cancelled
   (nothing built)

Changes in version 2.2.0
agent accuracy & control plane follow-ups (optional AI assistant):
 - WP8 semantic tools: set_enrichment_parameters (ORA/fGSEA panel) and
   set_table_view (feature/sample/expression tables: columns,
   multi-selection, per-column filters, page)
 - WP9 capability registry generated from the widget store + tool
   metadata; search_ui_capabilities / get_ui_capability discovery tools;
   state overview carries capability counts only
 - data tables register page + column filters on the widget store
   (DT proxy push; new "mapping" widget kind)
 - WP11 conversation-in-snapshot: opt-in .ESS persistence of the chat
   transcript, tool context, and figure registry with credential
   redaction and byte caps
 - WP12 session governance: optional OMICSVIEWER_LLM_MAX_COST_USD and
   OMICSVIEWER_LLM_MAX_TOKENS cumulative budgets (unlimited-but-logged
   by default); budget_limit joins the log-summarizer error taxonomy

Changes in version 2.1.78
bug fixes:
 - attr4: gene highlighting was dead - the searchon -> searchValue
   wiring was removed as "dead code", but debounce() in shiny >= 1.6
   installs a tracker observer that eagerly runs its argument, so the
   idiom really did write input$searchon into searchValue. Re-wired as
   observeEvent(input$searchon); unsetting the Search cascade now also
   clears params$highlight. New regression board
   tests/test_attr4SearchHighlight.R
 - STRING API repairs: safe_GET() with a NULL query no longer strips
   URL parameters (fixes the STRING 400); networkD3 ordinal legend
   scale fix for the enrichment table
 - PTMotif: .ggseqlogo_quiet() mutes ggseqlogo 0.2.2
   deprecated-ggplot2 warnings; geom_vline(size=) -> linewidth=
 - e2e: tracked Playwright regression guard
   tests/e2e_agent/verify_clear_area.mjs confirming "Clear figure
   selection" erases the scatter x/y area selection (volcano box-select
   then Clear, census of plotly select-outline/selectionlayer artifacts)

